Update ImageSharp and override vulnerable transitive dependencies consistently
across the application and its plugins, including native font/image libraries.

ImageSharp 3.2.0: https://github.com/SixLabors/ImageSharp/pull/3208
HarfBuzz: https://github.com/harfbuzz/harfbuzz/security/advisories/GHSA-q4gc-p4hh-3765
SkiaSharp: https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-j7hp-h8jx-5ppr
Tmds.DBus.Protocol: https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-xrw6-gwf8-vvr9

Retargeting to .NET 10 also removes the vulnerable System.Text.Json and
System.Private.Uri packages, whose APIs are provided by the framework.

UABEA is MIT-licensed and uses ImageSharp under the Apache-2.0 grant for
open-source applications in its Split License. Exclude the NuGet build-time
license-key tooling while retaining the compile/runtime assets.
https://github.com/SixLabors/ImageSharp/blob/v3.2.0/LICENSE

diff --git a/Directory.Build.props b/Directory.Build.props
new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
+++ b/Directory.Build.props
@@ -0,0 +1,17 @@
+<Project>
+  <PropertyGroup>
+    <!-- Solution builds need a RID on each project to generate apphosts. -->
+    <RuntimeIdentifier>linux-x64</RuntimeIdentifier>
+  </PropertyGroup>
+  <ItemGroup>
+    <!-- Override transitive packages in every project so publishing the solution
+         cannot overwrite a fixed assembly with an older one. -->
+    <PackageReference Include="HarfBuzzSharp" Version="14.4.0.100" />
+    <PackageReference Include="HarfBuzzSharp.NativeAssets.Linux" Version="14.4.0.100" />
+    <PackageReference Include="HarfBuzzSharp.NativeAssets.WebAssembly" Version="14.4.0.100" />
+    <PackageReference Include="SkiaSharp" Version="2.88.9" />
+    <PackageReference Include="SkiaSharp.NativeAssets.Linux" Version="2.88.9" />
+    <PackageReference Include="SkiaSharp.NativeAssets.WebAssembly" Version="2.88.9" />
+    <PackageReference Include="Tmds.DBus.Protocol" Version="0.21.3" />
+  </ItemGroup>
+</Project>
